TYPES.md §3.7, §15: the inferred type of a public `const` is exposed (constants are emitted in every mode): a local enum's member, or a list of them, is E2111 at the const's name, which has no type expression; a local const may hold anything.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local enum Cut { round, square }

/// The default cut.
const DEFAULT_CUT = Cut.round

/// Every cut.
const CUTS = [Cut.round, Cut.square]

/// A count.
const COUNT = 2

local const FIRST = Cut.square
-- findings.txt --
error[E2111]  a/a.canon:6:7
  DEFAULT_CUT is public but exposes the local type Cut: make Cut public or DEFAULT_CUT local

error[E2111]  a/a.canon:9:7
  CUTS is public but exposes the local type Cut: make Cut public or CUTS local

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
